 "notes": "Abu Kafan (Abu el Kefan), a narrow reef about 650 m long NNW-SSE standing alone in open water, with near-vertical walls on both long sides dropping far past 60 m and a plateau at 10-30 m off each end: the northern one with two coral blocks down its middle, the southern one with the erg joined to the reef at about 18 m. The plateaus and blocks are placed from dive-centre descriptions (4eversea, divers-guide.com), so their extent is approximate; the drift line is the usual plateau-to-plateau drift with the northerly current, not a recorded track.",
